'''''Phytolacca heterotepala''''', the '''Mexican pokeweed''', is a species of plant in the pokeweed family [[Phytolaccaceae]]. It is native to the state of [[Tamaulipas]] in northeast Mexico and has been introduced to the U.S. state of California and Portugal.<ref>{{cite web |title=World Plants: Complete Plant List |url=http://www.worldplants.de/?deeplink=Phytolacca-heterotepala |website=www.worldplants.de |access-date=10 November 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Phytolacca heterotepala H.Walter {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:195821-2 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=10 November 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

